          "body": "## What\n- `src/main.rs`: the full command surface from plan \u00a73.4 \u2014 `agents`, `board [--all|--to]`, `claim`, `heartbeat`, `release`, `note`, `stop`, `prs`, `run`, `doctor`, `serve`, `web`; bare `bf` calls `tui::run`. Exit codes: 0 ok \u00b7 1 error \u00b7 2 conflict/refusal \u00b7 3 not implemented (message names the plan PR) \u00b7 64 bad input. `bf web` keeps the old browser flow (spawn `serve`, exchange the bootstrap secret, print/open the URL; `xdg-open` only when `DISPLAY` is set).\n- `bf doctor` is now **lock-free** (no `Hub::open`, no database): data dir, SQLite version, gh auth, `--version` of claude/codex/cursor-agent/grok, node/npm vs the pins, and the caller's detected identity. It works while `bf serve` runs.\n- `src/identity.rs` (real): `--as`/`BF_AGENT` declared name plus the **observed** provider and pid from the `/proc` ancestor chain (exe under `~/.grok/` \u2192 grok; `cursor-agent/versions/` in cmdline \u2192 cursor; comm `codex`/`claude`), with fake-proc tests. A declared name never hides which process wrote (spec \u00a713).\n- Stubs with their final signatures so PRs 4/5/6 compile independently and touch one arm each: `src/agents.rs` (`Env`, `Agent`, `discover`, `plain_table`), `src/board.rs` (`cli_*`, `parse_ttl` real + tested), `src/prs.rs` (`Pr`, `list`), `src/tui/mod.rs` (`Source` trait, `Snapshot` + row types, `StubSource`, `plain`, `run`).\n- `Cargo.toml`: `ratatui =0.30.2` (crossterm feature only), `crossterm =0.29.0`, `clap` `env` feature, `reqwest` re-added for the `bf web` client (dropped in #3; the lean alternative is a hand-rolled loopback HTTP client \u2014 deferred to PR 10 when the page is rewritten).\n- `AGENTS.md`: the board rules and PR/review protocol for agents working in this repo.\n- `tests/cli_skeleton.rs`: `--help` lists every verb (and hides `demo`); `doctor` returns JSON with the SQLite pin; each unimplemented verb exits 3 and names its PR; bad input exits 64; bare `bf` without a tty prints the plain snapshot.\n\n## Acceptance (plan \u00a74, PR 3)\n- `bf --help` lists every \u00a73.4 verb \u2714 (test)\n- `bf doctor` prints sqlite + the four CLI versions \u2714 (test asserts `sqlite = 3.53.2`, `node_pin = v22.23.2`)\n- Branch protection on `main`: already applied and verified \u2014 `gh api repos/neverhuman/bf/branches/main/protection --jq .required_status_checks` \u2192 `{\"strict\":true,\"contexts\":[\"check\"]}`, linear history, no force-push, enforce admins.\n- Local `bash scripts/check` EXIT 0 in 28 s; isolated tree: clippy `-D warnings` clean, 16 tests green.\n\n## Review\nReviewer must be a different vendor (grok, codex or cursor). Post `REVIEW: approve <head-sha>` via `gh pr review --comment`, then `gh pr merge --rebase --delete-branch`.\n\nbf-author: claude/claude-orch\nbf-claim: AGENT_CHAT.md 2026-09-18T16:11Z\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
